        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "ea2a1f4c-547f-3247-86b0-628eb9f41cf4",
                "word": "placidity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "fa22e244-1751-4942-afbb-bc9bca693d30",
                        "entry_id": "ea2a1f4c-547f-3247-86b0-628eb9f41cf4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "placidities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "49f23c31-fb27-39b5-8154-2ccbbd1eb43e",
                        "entry_id": "ea2a1f4c-547f-3247-86b0-628eb9f41cf4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being placid; peacefulness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c94217a2-8203-4f62-b147-fe14f6ec648c",
                                "sense_id": "49f23c31-fb27-39b5-8154-2ccbbd1eb43e",
                                "text": "And how could she bear such behaviour! Composure with a witness! to look on, while repeated attentions were offering to another woman, before her face, and not resent it.—That is a degree of placidity, which I can neither comprehend nor respect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "218544af-306f-40ef-a1bc-a1f477c3c382",
                                "sense_id": "49f23c31-fb27-39b5-8154-2ccbbd1eb43e",
                                "text": "Thus, in rapid succession, passed the thoughts of Rosilia, who, endeavouring to assume placidity, once more essayed to express her thanks to Mrs. Melbourne for her kind attentions,[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1dba323-adc2-4f8b-b624-4dee6e70b8b5",
                                "sense_id": "49f23c31-fb27-39b5-8154-2ccbbd1eb43e",
                                "text": "The swift and indifferent placidity of that look troubled me."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c04714e-55e6-4f9c-86f1-69260d2513ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea2a1f4c-547f-3247-86b0-628eb9f41cf4",
                        "source_sense_id": "49f23c31-fb27-39b5-8154-2ccbbd1eb43e",
                        "source_sense_description": "state of being placid",
                        "target_lang_word": "placidité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "placidité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8faf360d-8fdf-3b46-8573-6891907807b2",
                                        "entry_id": "8f4d16c1-394b-3968-b439-9491738fc3f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Douceur naturelle ; caractère calme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "327f5f14-5f2f-4d74-a639-7d9a810ab02d",
                                                "sense_id": "8faf360d-8fdf-3b46-8573-6891907807b2",
                                                "text": "Ce fils de paysan, blêmi dans les soucis du commerce, gras de vie sédentaire, cachant ses appétits haineux sous la placidité naturelle de ses traits, avait en effet l’air nul et solennel, la carrure imbécile qui pose un homme dans un salon officiel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b038a172-50c9-405d-91d2-8ac2b7e2ffae",
                                                "sense_id": "8faf360d-8fdf-3b46-8573-6891907807b2",
                                                "text": "La falaise … vous écrasait de sa placidité formidable et elle vous charmait pourtant ; car on la contemplait malgré soi et les yeux ne s’en lassaient pas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9095939b-1df0-4f53-adc6-5722ca61bc94",
                                                "sense_id": "8faf360d-8fdf-3b46-8573-6891907807b2",
                                                "text": "Alors, il faudra que moi j’attende ce jugement aux Cinq-Fontaines, entre ton Oncle, qui me narguera, et Adalbert qui ne se fera pas de bile et dont la placidité me mettra hors de moi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ddf64d4-ee86-45e3-95a8-676ae423b5f8",
                                                "sense_id": "8faf360d-8fdf-3b46-8573-6891907807b2",
                                                "text": "Malgré sa corpulence excessive, l’autorité de M. Hector sur ses subordonnés n’est guère contestable. Il la doit surtout à sa placidité étudiée, au ton solennel et ampoulé qu’il affecte en s’exprimant, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
